Title: THE SHERLOCK HOLMES CIPHER
Credit: Written by
Author: Arthur Conan
Draft date: 2026-08-03

EXT. 221B BAKER STREET - DAY

A thick London fog hangs over Baker Street. A horse-drawn Hansom cab rattles down the cobblestone road.

INT. 221B BAKER STREET - SITTING ROOM - DAY

SHERLOCK HOLMES sits by the fireplace, examining a ciphered letter through a magnifying glass.

DR. JOHN WATSON enters carrying morning tea.

WATSON
Any progress on the Moriarty cipher, Holmes?

HOLMES
It is a double transposition, Watson. Intricate, but not unsolvable.

EXT. COVENT GARDEN MARKET - DAY

WATSON and IRENE ADLER hurry through the crowded market stalls.

IRENE
He was seen heading toward the docks!

INT. TOWER BRIDGE WAREHOUSE - NIGHT

HOLMES stands in the shadows of the deserted wharf warehouse.

PROFESSOR MORIARTY emerges from behind a stack of crates.

MORIARTY
You are persistent, Mr. Holmes. But this evening ends here.

Holmes draws his revolver as fog rolls through the open bay doors.
